WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.230
Cupertino, California.

2
00:00:02.280 --> 00:00:06.970
Apple's headquarters, and
about 166,000 employees.

3
00:00:07.020 --> 00:00:14.090
In the year to September 2025, Apple's
net sales were 416.2 billion dollars.

4
00:00:14.140 --> 00:00:18.330
Toyota sells vehicles in about
200 countries and regions.

5
00:00:18.380 --> 00:00:22.950
With its affiliates, it runs over 50
manufacturing operations outside Japan,

6
00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:26.350
in 27 different countries and regions.

7
00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:30.590
Why do these two giants make their
products in such different ways?

8
00:00:30.640 --> 00:00:32.750
Can't Apple afford factories?

9
00:00:32.800 --> 00:00:36.370
In this mission, you'll learn the
language of global production:

10
00:00:36.420 --> 00:00:40.170
foreign direct investment,
outsourcing and offshoring.

11
00:00:40.220 --> 00:00:42.270
Then you'll read both firms' own reports,

12
00:00:42.320 --> 00:00:45.550
and test Toyota's Just in Time system.

13
00:00:45.600 --> 00:00:50.290
Your mission: explain why Apple and Toyota
make their products in such different

14
00:00:50.340 --> 00:00:50.990
ways.
